//====================================================
// ESP32 GAME STATION
// SHARED GAME-AI PERCEPTION AND WORLD SNAPSHOT CONTRACT
// 129_ai_perception_system.h
//====================================================
//
// Responsibilities:
// - Converts game-world stimuli into bounded AI observations.
// - Supports vision, hearing, contact and game-rule information.
// - Tracks recently perceived entities without dynamic allocation.
// - Applies fair confidence decay and limited prediction over time.
// - Provides nearest-target and highest-threat queries to later AI.
// - Keeps hidden game state unavailable unless the game explicitly
//   submits it through an allowed perception channel.
//
// Fair-play rule:
// - Difficulty may alter reaction delay, memory and prediction quality,
//   but this system never scans game state by itself. Each game decides
//   which stimuli are legally observable and submits only those values.
//
// Coordinate rule:
// - Positions and velocities use game-defined signed world units.
// - Every value inside one perception frame must use the same scale.
// - Distance calculations use 64-bit intermediates in file 130.
//
// Integration rule:
// - File 130 implements this contract.
// - Later target-selection, steering and tactics systems query the
//   immutable observation records produced here.
// - No heap allocation or floating-point arithmetic is required.
//====================================================

